  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The implementation of EAC has killed free modded clients. Modded clients that allow Linux players to play, full body users to look good, fan films that rely on the camera mods to the camera in vrc actually usable, and many more uses. I think the best solution would be to put mod support directly into the game, you could have trusted users or maybe even a further rank that could even volunteer to verify mods because just from the backlash you can tell that a lot of people rely on these mods. On top of that whitelisting virtual machine which just runs virtual os's because that is how our Linux player plays. Getting rid of malicious clients and rippers is great, but a lot of those clients are already finding workarounds. You could send a cease and desist to the ripper store and the rippers are still going to exist because of huge laps in security because you can grab the information directly from the URL",
